From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:10:51 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iio: imu: Add Apple AOP accelerometer and
 gyroscope

The Always-On Processor of Apple laptops reads the machine's inertial
sensor and reports acceleration and angular rate as two services. Describe
their child nodes, and allow them under the T6041 AOP.

A service starts reporting only once it has been sent the machine's three
calibration packets. They are machine data from the Apple device tree, so
the bootloader fills them in at every boot and the device tree sources
carry none.

Based on Eryk Wieliczko's J713 work (dirtyroom-linux 63e6467a).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 2490d944a25ca23d65f4358fa4d0e0f4e2c796fa)
---
